# Resume Builder - Cursor Rules
You are building a resume builder SaaS platform.

## Tech Stack
- Frontend: Next.js 15, React 19, TypeScript, Tailwind CSS, Redux Toolkit
- Backend: Express.js, TypeScript, Prisma ORM
- Database: PostgreSQL (Neon)
- Cache: Upstash Redis
- Auth: Clerk
- Payments: Stripe + Razorpay
- AI: OpenAI GPT-4
- Storage: Supabase Storage
- Deployment: Vercel

## Architecture Principles
- Use TypeScript strictly (no `any` types)
- Implement AES-256 encryption for sensitive data
- All API routes must have rate limiting
- Follow Prisma ORM for all DB queries
- Use Redux for credit/payment state management
- Implement input validation with Zod

## Security Requirements
- Password hashing with Argon2
- JWT tokens with httpOnly cookies
- HTTPS/TLS for all connections
- Data encryption at rest (AES-256)
- Sanitize all file uploads

## API Conventions
- Use TypeScript types for all endpoints
- Return structured error responses
- Implement proper HTTP status codes
- Add request logging for security audits

## File Structure
- /pages for Next.js routes
- /pages/api for backend API
- /components for React components
- /lib for utilities
- /prisma for database schema
- /middleware for authentication


## Error Handling & Logging
**Critical Rule: NO silent fallbacks, NO graceful degradation that masks underlying issues.
- NEVER use fallback data that could hide the real problem
- ALWAYS raise an exception with detailed context
- ALWAYS log the full error with all relevant parameters
- ALWAYS make the failure obvious to the developer
